From cd82d911b14eed1f918788afd921c2a4b2f59f74 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Klemens Arro <1125090+kempu@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 18:30:24 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] email ingest: keep a message the account's Sieve script
 marked $notjunk in the Inbox

Delivery files a message the spam filter classified as spam into Junk
when it is headed for the Inbox. A Sieve script could not keep one out:
`fileinto "INBOX"` resolves to the same destination as an implicit keep,
so it was re-routed too. An organisation that trusts a sender therefore
had no way to say "never treat this sender's mail as spam" from the
account's script, and its trusted senders' mail still landed in Junk.

Skip the re-route when the message carries $notjunk, the keyword a
script sets with `addflag "$notjunk"`. A sender cannot set a keyword
over SMTP; only the script the account owner or an administrator
installed can. Every other spam message bound for the Inbox still goes
to Junk with $junk, and nothing about classification or training
changes.
---
 crates/email/src/message/ingest.rs | 11 ++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/crates/email/src/message/ingest.rs b/crates/email/src/message/ingest.rs
index 7538ee4..189233c 100644
--- a/crates/email/src/message/ingest.rs
+++ b/crates/email/src/message/ingest.rs
@@ -354,7 +354,16 @@ impl EmailIngest for Server {
                         offset_end: extra_headers.len() as u32,
                     });
 
-                    if is_spam && params.mailbox_ids == [INBOX_ID] {
+                    // Spam headed for the Inbox goes to Junk, unless the account's own Sieve
+                    // script marked it $notjunk. That keyword is the only way a script can keep
+                    // a message the filter scored as spam out of Junk: `fileinto "INBOX"`
+                    // resolves to the same destination as an implicit keep, and so is re-routed
+                    // here too. A sender cannot set a keyword over SMTP; only the script the
+                    // account owner or an administrator installed can.
+                    if is_spam
+                        && params.mailbox_ids == [INBOX_ID]
+                        && !params.keywords.contains(&Keyword::NotJunk)
+                    {
                         params.mailbox_ids[0] = JUNK_ID;
                         params.keywords.push(Keyword::Junk);
                     }
